{"type":"message","id":"0be29cef","parentId":"1de60d8f","timestamp":"2026-04-24T13:34:12.074Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found 赵晨旭. Now I need to understand the question better. The user asked \"你可以和赵晨旭的openclaw拉到一个群聊里吗\" - this means \"Can you and Zhao Chenxu's OpenClaw be pulled into a group chat?\"\n\nThis likely means: can two OpenClaw bots (the user's bot and Zhao Chenxu's bot) be in the same group chat together? Or does the user want to create a group chat that includes both bots?\n\nI should explain what I can do:\n- I can create a group chat and add members (including bots if I know their App IDs)\n\n\n- The tricky part is that I don't have Zhao Chenxu's OpenClaw bot information, so I'd need the bot's App ID to add it to a group. Also, there's a distinction in Feishu between bot accounts and regular user accounts when it comes to group management that I should clarify with the user. I'm realizing I need to ask the user for Zhao Chenxu's OpenClaw bot ID or app ID before I can proceed with adding it to a group chat.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n找到赵晨旭了！\n\n不过要把我（你的机器人）和赵晨旭的 OpenClaw 拉进同一个群，需要知道对方的 **App ID** 才能操作。\n\n你手上有赵晨旭的 OpenClaw App ID 吗？或者问一下赵晨旭他的机器人的 App ID 是什么，把那个 ID 发给我，我就能创建群聊把我们俩都加进去～ 🦞"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"miaoda","model":"miaoda-model-auto","usage":{"input":688,"output":309,"cacheRead":46139,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47136,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777037640512,"responseId":"chatcmpl-2249a6c7-3713-47e2-8c6b-8397e2b8b706"}}
