{"type":"message","id":"2269ea93","parentId":"f83bac8e","timestamp":"2026-04-24T13:35:11.442Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check what commands are available in lark-cli.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_kbtnwkvntsnl_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"lark-cli --help 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"miaoda","model":"miaoda-model-auto","usage":{"input":339,"output":56,"cacheRead":47483,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47878,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777037708314,"responseId":"chatcmpl-3b8f8caa-4bf3-4f29-8471-ad1d9dcf3cd6"}}
{"type":"message","id":"948e6ba5","parentId":"2269ea93","timestamp":"2026-04-24T13:35:11.621Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_kbtnwkvntsnl_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"lark-cli — Lark/Feishu CLI tool.\n\nUSAGE:\n    lark-cli <command> [subcommand] [method] [options]\n    lark-cli api <method> <path> [--params <json>] [--data <json>]\n    lark-cli schema <service.resource.method> [--format pretty]\n\nEXAMPLES:\n    # View upcoming events\n    lark-cli calendar +agenda\n\n    # List calendar events\n    lark-cli calendar events instance_view --params '{\"calendar_id\":\"primary\",\"start_time\":\"1700000000\",\"end_time\":\"1700086400\"}'\n\n    # Search users\n    lark-cli contact +search-user --query \"John\"\n\n    # Generic API call\n    lark-cli api GET /open-apis/calendar/v4/calendars\n\nFLAGS:\n    --params <json>       URL/query parameters JSON\n    --data <json>         request body JSON (POST/PATCH/PUT/DELETE)\n    --as <type>           identity type: user | bot | auto (default: auto)\n    --format <fmt>        output format: json (default) | ndjson | table | csv | pretty\n    --page-all            automatically paginate through all pages\n    --page-size <N>       page size (0 = use API default)\n    --page-limit <N>      max pages to fetch with --page-all (default: 10, 0 for unlimited)\n    --page-delay <MS>     delay in ms between pages (default: 200, only with --page-all)\n    -o, --output <path>   output file path for binary responses\n    --jq <expr>           jq expression to filter JSON output\n    -q <expr>             shorthand for --jq\n    --dry-run             print request without executing\n\nAI AGENT SKILLS:\n    lark-cli pairs with AI agent skills (Claude Code, etc.) that\n    teach the agent Lark API patterns, best practices, and workflows.\n\n    Install all skills:\n        npx skills add larksuite/cli -g -y\n\n    Or pick specific domains:\n        npx skills add larksuite/cli -s lark-calendar -y\n        npx skills add larksuite/cli -s lark-im -y\n\n    Learn more: https://github.com/larksuite/cli#agent-skills\n\nCOMMUNITY:\n    GitHub:     https://github.com/larksuite/cli\n    Issues:     https://github.com/larksuite/cli/issues\n    Docs:       https://open.feishu.cn/document/\n\nMore help: lark-cli <command> --help\n\nUsage:\n  lark-cli [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  api         Generic Lark API requests\n  attendance  attendance record query\n  auth        OAuth credentials and authorization management\n  base        Table, field, record, view, dashboard, workflow, form, role & permission management\n  calendar    Calendar, event, and attendee management\n  config      Global CLI configuration management\n  contact     Contacts operations\n  docs        Document and content operations\n  doctor      CLI health check: config, auth, and connectivity\n  drive       File, comment, permission, and upload management\n  event       Event subscription management\n  help        Help about any command\n  im          Message and group chat management\n  mail        Email, draft, folder, and contacts management\n  minutes     Minutes content and metadata retrieval\n  okr         Lark OKR objectives, key results, alignments, indicators\n  profile     Manage configuration profiles\n  schema      View API method parameters, types, and scopes\n  sheets      Spreadsheet operations\n  slides      Create and manage presentations, read content, and add or remove slides\n  task        Task, task list, and subtask management\n  update      Update lark-cli to the latest version\n  vc          Video conference and meeting note management\n  whiteboard  Create and edit boards\n  wiki        Wiki space and node management\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for lark-cli\n      --profile string   use a specific profile\n  -v, --version          version for lark-cli\n\nUse \"lark-cli [command] --help\" for more information about a command."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":61,"aggregated":"lark-cli — Lark/Feishu CLI tool.\n\nUSAGE:\n    lark-cli <command> [subcommand] [method] [options]\n    lark-cli api <method> <path> [--params <json>] [--data <json>]\n    lark-cli schema <service.resource.method> [--format pretty]\n\nEXAMPLES:\n    # View upcoming events\n    lark-cli calendar +agenda\n\n    # List calendar events\n    lark-cli calendar events instance_view --params '{\"calendar_id\":\"primary\",\"start_time\":\"1700000000\",\"end_time\":\"1700086400\"}'\n\n    # Search users\n    lark-cli contact +search-user --query \"John\"\n\n    # Generic API call\n    lark-cli api GET /open-apis/calendar/v4/calendars\n\nFLAGS:\n    --params <json>       URL/query parameters JSON\n    --data <json>         request body JSON (POST/PATCH/PUT/DELETE)\n    --as <type>           identity type: user | bot | auto (default: auto)\n    --format <fmt>        output format: json (default) | ndjson | table | csv | pretty\n    --page-all            automatically paginate through all pages\n    --page-size <N>       page size (0 = use API default)\n    --page-limit <N>      max pages to fetch with --page-all (default: 10, 0 for unlimited)\n    --page-delay <MS>     delay in ms between pages (default: 200, only with --page-all)\n    -o, --output <path>   output file path for binary responses\n    --jq <expr>           jq expression to filter JSON output\n    -q <expr>             shorthand for --jq\n    --dry-run             print request without executing\n\nAI AGENT SKILLS:\n    lark-cli pairs with AI agent skills (Claude Code, etc.) that\n    teach the agent Lark API patterns, best practices, and workflows.\n\n    Install all skills:\n        npx skills add larksuite/cli -g -y\n\n    Or pick specific domains:\n        npx skills add larksuite/cli -s lark-calendar -y\n        npx skills add larksuite/cli -s lark-im -y\n\n    Learn more: https://github.com/larksuite/cli#agent-skills\n\nCOMMUNITY:\n    GitHub:     https://github.com/larksuite/cli\n    Issues:     https://github.com/larksuite/cli/issues\n    Docs:       https://open.feishu.cn/document/\n\nMore help: lark-cli <command> --help\n\nUsage:\n  lark-cli [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  api         Generic Lark API requests\n  attendance  attendance record query\n  auth        OAuth credentials and authorization management\n  base        Table, field, record, view, dashboard, workflow, form, role & permission management\n  calendar    Calendar, event, and attendee management\n  config      Global CLI configuration management\n  contact     Contacts operations\n  docs        Document and content operations\n  doctor      CLI health check: config, auth, and connectivity\n  drive       File, comment, permission, and upload management\n  event       Event subscription management\n  help        Help about any command\n  im          Message and group chat management\n  mail        Email, draft, folder, and contacts management\n  minutes     Minutes content and metadata retrieval\n  okr         Lark OKR objectives, key results, alignments, indicators\n  profile     Manage configuration profiles\n  schema      View API method parameters, types, and scopes\n  sheets      Spreadsheet operations\n  slides      Create and manage presentations, read content, and add or remove slides\n  task        Task, task list, and subtask management\n  update      Update lark-cli to the latest version\n  vc          Video conference and meeting note management\n  whiteboard  Create and edit boards\n  wiki        Wiki space and node management\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for lark-cli\n      --profile string   use a specific profile\n  -v, --version          version for lark-cli\n\nUse \"lark-cli [command] --help\" for more information about a command.","cwd":"/home/gem/workspace/agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777037711617}}
{"type":"message","id":"2dbb6218","parentId":"948e6ba5","timestamp":"2026-04-24T13:35:17.167Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see that `lark-cli im` is for message and group chat management. Let me check how to create a group chat.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_nn1c3xilwy0y_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"lark-cli im --help 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"miaoda","model":"miaoda-model-auto","usage":{"input":48772,"output":73,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48845,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777037711622,"responseId":"chatcmpl-11dde85e-187d-467d-9a3b-f892afb6e6af"}}
{"type":"message","id":"76689cfd","parentId":"2dbb6218","timestamp":"2026-04-24T13:35:17.420Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_nn1c3xilwy0y_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Message and group chat management\n\nUsage:\n  lark-cli im [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  +chat-create                 Create a group chat; user/bot; creates private/public chats, invites users/bots, optionally sets bot manager\n  +chat-messages-list          List messages in a chat or P2P conversation; user/bot; accepts --chat-id or --user-id, resolves P2P chat_id, supports time range/sort/pagination\n  +chat-search                 Search visible group chats by keyword and/or member open_ids (e.g. look up chat_id by group name); user/bot; supports member/type filters, sorting, and pagination\n  +chat-update                 Update group chat name or description; user/bot; updates a chat's name or description\n  +messages-mget               Batch get messages by IDs; user/bot; fetches up to 50 om_ message IDs, formats sender names, expands thread replies\n  +messages-reply              Reply to a message (supports thread replies); user/bot; supports text/markdown/post/media replies, reply-in-thread, idempotency key\n  +messages-resources-download Download images/files from a message; user/bot; downloads image/file resources by message-id and file-key to a safe relative output path\n  +messages-send               Send a message to a chat or direct message; user/bot; sends to chat-id or user-id with text/markdown/post/media, supports idempotency key\n  +threads-messages-list       List messages in a thread; user/bot; accepts om_/omt_ input, resolves message IDs to thread_id, supports sort/pagination\n  chat.members                 chat.members operations\n  chats                        chats operations\n  images                       images operations\n  messages                     messages operations\n  pins                         pins operations\n  reactions                    reactions operations\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for im\n\nUse \"lark-cli im [command] --help\" for more information about a command."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":102,"aggregated":"Message and group chat management\n\nUsage:\n  lark-cli im [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  +chat-create                 Create a group chat; user/bot; creates private/public chats, invites users/bots, optionally sets bot manager\n  +chat-messages-list          List messages in a chat or P2P conversation; user/bot; accepts --chat-id or --user-id, resolves P2P chat_id, supports time range/sort/pagination\n  +chat-search                 Search visible group chats by keyword and/or member open_ids (e.g. look up chat_id by group name); user/bot; supports member/type filters, sorting, and pagination\n  +chat-update                 Update group chat name or description; user/bot; updates a chat's name or description\n  +messages-mget               Batch get messages by IDs; user/bot; fetches up to 50 om_ message IDs, formats sender names, expands thread replies\n  +messages-reply              Reply to a message (supports thread replies); user/bot; supports text/markdown/post/media replies, reply-in-thread, idempotency key\n  +messages-resources-download Download images/files from a message; user/bot; downloads image/file resources by message-id and file-key to a safe relative output path\n  +messages-send               Send a message to a chat or direct message; user/bot; sends to chat-id or user-id with text/markdown/post/media, supports idempotency key\n  +threads-messages-list       List messages in a thread; user/bot; accepts om_/omt_ input, resolves message IDs to thread_id, supports sort/pagination\n  chat.members                 chat.members operations\n  chats                        chats operations\n  images                       images operations\n  messages                     messages operations\n  pins                         pins operations\n  reactions                    reactions operations\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for im\n\nUse \"lark-cli im [command] --help\" for more information about a command.","cwd":"/home/gem/workspace/agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777037717416}}
